{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The re-propose protection is measured: the client request is re-queued while the owner's instance takes the NOOP. Submitting that."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Submitted a probe for the client-completion mechanism that surrounds the recovery value replacement: the owner stays alive, its accepted command is replaced by the recovery's NOOP commit, and the harness records whether handleCommit re-queues the pending client request and whether any reply was produced for the original instance. A new source range covers the re-propose block, and a new question records the completion-contract relationship.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-commit-repropose\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"epaxos/epaxos.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1082,\\\"end_line\\\":1100,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@k-commit-requeues-pending-proposal\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"handleCommit, for the instance owner only, tests whether the committed command is a single NONE operation and whether the local leader bookkeeping still holds pending client proposals; when both hold it pushes every pending proposal back onto the replica's own ProposeChan and clears lb.clientProposals, so the client request is re-proposed on a new instance instead of being consumed by the committed NOOP.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"A commit that decides a single NOOP for an instance owned by the local replica while that replica still holds client proposals for it (epaxos/epaxos.go:1082-1100, reached after a recovery replaced the owner's accepted command).\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-commit-repropose\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\"]}],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@rec-client-requeue\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"When a recovery replaces the command that a live owner had proposed and accepted locally, does the owner's client request survive through the re-propose path, and does the original instance produce any reply?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-commit-repropose\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"handleCommit re-queues the pending proposals on the owner's ProposeChan and clears them, so the client's request is not silently consumed by the replacement decision, but the original instance produces no reply because replies are emitted only when the state machine executes commands and the executed command is the NOOP.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether the owner's propose channel receives exactly the pending proposal with the same command id while the owner's instance ends COMMITTED with the NOOP, and whether the reply writer for that proposal received no bytes.\\\",\n  \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\"}],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@rec-client-requeue\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\"./epaxos\\\",\n  \\\"test_names\\\":[\\\"TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoveryReproposesClientRequest\\\"],\n  \\\"anchors\\\":[{\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startRecoveryForInstance\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1127,\\\"end_line\\\":1141}],\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-commit-repropose\\\",\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Five replicas (F=2) in the existing harness. Owner replica 0 proposes command X with a real defs.GPropose attached (command id 77, reply writer over a local buffer); replica 1 holds a conflicting command so its pre-accept reply is non-equal, and replica 1 fails after replying; replica 3, which holds no command, recovers instance (0,0) while the owner is still alive; the quiescent exchange is completed; the owner's propose channel is then drained and its instance state, pending proposals and reply writer size are recorded.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n    \\\"Same construction, transport boundary and crash model as the other experiments in this harness.\\\",\n    \\\"The owner stays alive throughout, modelling a slow but reachable owner whose instance is decided by another replica's recovery.\\\",\n    \\\"No executor goroutine runs, so any reply observed would have to come from the recovery/handleCommit paths rather than from the state-machine execution path.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No run() loop, no executeCommands goroutine and no client socket; the client request is supplied as the target's own defs.GPropose value.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"n\\\":5,\\\"f\\\":2,\\\"owner\\\":0,\\\"recoverer\\\":3,\\\"command_id\\\":77,\\\"value_key\\\":1}\n  },\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness attaches a real GPropose to the owner's startPhase1 call, drives the conflicting premise and the owner's non-equal pre-accept reply, fails replica 1, calls startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) at replica 3, delivers the emitted Prepare/PrepareReply/PreAccept traffic and the resulting Commit through the target's handlers, and finally drains the owner's ProposeChan while recording the owner's instance status, committed command, remaining pending proposals and reply buffer size.\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A committed replacement decision for an instance must not silently consume the client request the owner had pending for it: the pending proposal must be re-offered for a new decision, and the client must not be told the original request completed.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The owner's own commit handling (epaxos/epaxos.go:1082-1100) and the recovery that produced the replacement decision (epaxos/epaxos.go:1236-1313); the client request was admitted through the replica's own propose path.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"owner-proposal\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"owner_proposal\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"command_id\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":77}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"owner-held-command\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_preaccept_replies\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"recovery-proposed-replacement\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_proposal\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"requeue_summary\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"replica\\\",\\\"instance_row\\\",\\\"instance_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"owner-proposal\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"requeued\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"owner_instance_status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"owner_cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The owner's pending client request is re-queued exactly once after its instance was decided with the replacement NOOP; violated when no proposal arrives on the owner's propose channel.\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(u,open('draft/update13.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update13.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
